# Relay Bazel configuration.

# ── Reproducible external deps (Lean toolchain, Mathlib, …) ───────────
# Downloaded archives (e.g. the Lean 4 toolchain tarball) are cached here
# so rebuilds / CI reuse them instead of re-downloading. Machine-local
# (not in git); the *inputs* are pinned (see MODULE.bazel + proofs/lean).
common --repository_cache=~/.cache/relay-bazel/repo

# Build-output cache (incl. compiled Mathlib-dependent proofs).
build --disk_cache=~/.cache/relay-bazel/disk

# ── Offline vendoring (redo the Lean/Mathlib build without network) ───
# Populate the vendor dir (Lean toolchain + Mathlib oleans + repos) with:
#   bazel vendor //proofs/lean:all --vendor_dir=vendor/bazel
# (or run proofs/lean/vendor.sh). Then build fully offline by adding:
#   common --vendor_dir=vendor/bazel
# The vendor dir is gitignored (multi-GB Mathlib oleans); it is
# regeneratable from the pinned versions, so "redo if needed" = re-run
# the vendor command. See proofs/lean/README.md.
